E_anom = y^2 = x^3 - 275 x + 1750, conductor 800
MW: rank 1, generator P = [-15, 50], torsion T = [10, 0] (Z/2)

=== Integral points among nP + eps*T, |n| up to 8 ===
  -2*P      = [46, 294]   [INTEGRAL]
  -1*P      = [-15, -50]   [INTEGRAL]
  -1*P + T  = [9, 2]   [INTEGRAL]
  0*P + T  = [10, 0]   [INTEGRAL]
  1*P      = [-15, 50]   [INTEGRAL]
  1*P + T  = [9, -2]   [INTEGRAL]
  2*P      = [46, -294]   [INTEGRAL]

=== Completeness via canonical heights ===
hat-h(P) = 0.94974108626589779505360275479729895984
   hat-h(1P) = n^2*hat-h(P) = 0.94974108626589779505360275479729895984
   hat-h(2P) = n^2*hat-h(P) = 3.7989643450635911802144110191891958394
   hat-h(3P) = n^2*hat-h(P) = 8.5476697763930801554824247931756906386
   hat-h(4P) = n^2*hat-h(P) = 15.195857380254364720857644076756783358
   hat-h(5P) = n^2*hat-h(P) = 23.743527156647444876340068869932473996
   hat-h(6P) = n^2*hat-h(P) = 34.190679105572320621929699172702762554
Torsion T adds 0 to canonical height; hat-h(nP + eps T) = n^2 hat-h(P).

x-denominators of nP and nP+T for n=3..6 (non-integral => not int. pts):
   n=3:  denom(x(nP))=3721   denom(x(nP+T))=1369
   n=4:  denom(x(nP))=345744   denom(x(nP+T))=1615441
   n=5:  denom(x(nP))=28284848761   denom(x(nP+T))=2809530025
   n=6:  denom(x(nP))=117317991183649   denom(x(nP+T))=68096263186116

=== Exhaustive bounded ellratpoints (naive height <= 10^7) ===
integral points by brute force (height<=10^7) = 7
   [-15, -50]
   [-15, 50]
   [9, -2]
   [9, 2]
   [10, 0]
   [46, -294]
   [46, 294]

=== Manual on-curve checks (framework's listed integral points) ===
   x=-15: x^3-275x+1750 = 2500 = 50^2 ? 1
   x=46: x^3-275x+1750 = 86436 = 294^2 ? 1
   x=9: x^3-275x+1750 = 4 = 2^2 ? 1
   x=10: x^3-275x+1750 = 0 = 0^2 ? 1
